1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,700
In today’s lecture, I’m going to be talking about microplastics.

2
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:12,770
Microplastics are tiny pieces of plastic smaller than five millimetres in size.

3
00:00:12,770 --> 00:00:18,196
Recently there’s been a greater awareness that there are large quantities of plastic waste – big

4
00:00:18,196 --> 00:00:21,210
and small – in the environment.

5
00:00:21,210 --> 00:00:26,100
The amount of plastic waste in the oceans has received widespread attention,

6
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:31,311
but far less is known about the effects of microplastics in freshwater

7
00:00:31,311 --> 00:00:35,520
and particularly in soil.

8
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:41,270
Microplastics can enter the environment via a number of different sources.

9
00:00:41,270 --> 00:00:48,088
Threads and microfibres detach from synthetic clothing every time they’re put in a washing

10
00:00:48,088 --> 00:00:48,870
machine,

11
00:00:48,870 --> 00:00:52,640
and these find their way into the water system.

12
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:58,098
Other sources include big pieces of plastic waste that are already in the environment,

13
00:00:58,098 --> 00:01:04,980
and these break down into microscopic particles over a period of time.

14
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:12,424
On a larger scale, factory waste is another route, as are tyres which wear down as cars, lorries

15
00:01:12,424 --> 00:01:17,400
and so on travel along road surfaces.

16
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:23,102
We already understand some of the impacts of microplastics from studies involving fish

17
00:01:23,102 --> 00:01:25,330
and other animals.

18
00:01:25,330 --> 00:01:32,121
There is evidence that microplastics harm small creatures in a variety of ways, such

19
00:01:32,121 --> 00:01:34,004
as by damaging their mouths,

20
00:01:34,004 --> 00:01:40,594
or by impairing their ability to feed, for example when microplastics get lodged in

21
00:01:40,594 --> 00:01:44,180
their digestive system.

22
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:50,478
Surprisingly perhaps, it is likely that humans consume microplastics, as these have been detected

23
00:01:50,478 --> 00:01:55,372
in a wide range of food and drink products, including bottled water, as well

24
00:01:55,372 --> 00:01:58,320
as in water that comes direct from the tap.

25
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:06,540
What’s more, salt and many kinds of seafood have also been found to contain

26
00:02:06,540 --> 00:02:06,590
microplastics.

27
00:02:06,590 --> 00:02:13,028
However, it’s important to underline that there is not yet conclusive proof that microplastics

28
00:02:13,028 --> 00:02:15,940
cause significant harm to people.

29
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:22,258
In many countries, including here in the UK, there is legislation which prevents manufacturers

30
00:02:22,258 --> 00:02:29,740
from adding plastic microbeads to shower gels, facial cleansers and toothpaste.

31
00:02:29,740 --> 00:02:35,772
It is very difficult to accurately estimate the total amount of microplastic particles in

32
00:02:35,772 --> 00:02:38,517
the soil as they can be hard to detect,

33
00:02:38,517 --> 00:02:41,624
but we do know they are carried in the air

34
00:02:41,624 --> 00:02:44,890
and deposited in the soil by rain.

35
00:02:44,890 --> 00:02:49,688
What’s more, many of the fertilisers used by both farmers

36
00:02:49,688 --> 00:02:55,410
and gardeners contain microplastics.

37
00:02:55,410 --> 00:03:00,188
A team from the Anglia Ruskin University in Cambridge has carried out a study

38
00:03:00,188 --> 00:03:05,790
of the effects of microplastics on the digestive tracts of earthworms.

39
00:03:05,790 --> 00:03:06,574
These worms,

40
00:03:06,574 --> 00:03:13,530
which live in topsoil, are an essential component of our agricultural system.

41
00:03:13,530 --> 00:03:21,130
By feeding on soil, they mix nutrients into it, thereby making it more fertile.

42
00:03:21,130 --> 00:03:26,041
The researchers set out to discover whether the introduction of microplastics into the soil–

43
00:03:26,041 --> 00:03:30,731
and the subsequent ingestion of these by earthworms – would impact soil quality

44
00:03:30,731 --> 00:03:35,040
and ultimately inhibit plant growth.

45
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:37,570
The short answer was, yes, it did.

46
00:03:37,570 --> 00:03:44,102
After placing three different types of microplastic particles into the soil, they planted perennial

47
00:03:44,102 --> 00:03:45,670
rye grass.

48
00:03:45,670 --> 00:03:47,374
The particles of microplastic,

49
00:03:47,374 --> 00:03:52,527
which included biodegradable PLA and conventional high-density polyethylene,

50
00:03:52,527 --> 00:03:57,820
or HDPE, were then ingested by the earthworms in the soil.

51
00:03:57,820 --> 00:04:01,290
The result was that the worms lost weight rapidly.

52
00:04:01,290 --> 00:04:06,183
What’s more, a lower percentage than normal of the rye grass seeds germinated,

53
00:04:06,183 --> 00:04:11,016
and the researchers concluded that this was a direct result of the earthworms being

54
00:04:11,016 --> 00:04:16,170
unable to fulfil their normal role in making soil more fertile.

55
00:04:16,170 --> 00:04:20,039
The team also discovered that there was an increase in the amount of acid

56
00:04:20,039 --> 00:04:21,021
found in the soil,

57
00:04:21,021 --> 00:04:29,780
and this was attributed mainly to the microplastic particles from conventional HDPE plastic.

58
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:34,902
The conclusions of the study make for very interesting reading – I’ve included the

59
00:04:34,902 --> 00:04:39,120
reference in the notes to give you at the end of this session.

60
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:44,378
To summarise, the authors proposed the idea that we need to regard soil as

61
00:04:44,378 --> 00:04:47,810
we would regard any other process in nature.

62
00:04:47,810 --> 00:04:53,106
This means we should accept the implications of soil being dependent on decaying

63
00:04:53,106 --> 00:04:57,680
and dead matter constantly being passed through the bodies of earthworms.

64
00:04:57,680 --> 00:04:58,042
That is,

65
00:04:58,042 --> 00:05:03,869
when soil becomes impoverished by the presence of microplastics, not only ecosystems

66
00:05:03,869 --> 00:05:08,290
but also the whole of society are negatively impacted.
